{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The resin release tape complements the epoxy resin I bought by helping with mold release and surface protection, so it supports a project I already have supplies for.",
    "The tool hooks fit my repeated purchases of workshop tools and supplies because keeping frequently used tools accessible would make that work easier."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The solenoid valve, pipe fitting and aluminum rails require specific projects, connections or dimensions that my purchases do not establish a need for.",
    "The drink mixing glass does not support my current workshop tasks, while more screw kits and a five-pack of spray bottles offer limited immediate value when I already have fasteners and no current need for that many bottles."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Buying workshop supplies seems to have been taken as a reason to suggest specialized hardware without knowing whether I need its particular function or specifications.",
    "My repeated fastener purchases seem to have been treated as a continuing need for more assortments, even though those purchases may already cover the sizes I use."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Supplies that help me use what I already own, such as release tape for my epoxy, feel more useful than equipment that starts an unrelated project.",
    "For fasteners, the missing size, required length and stock I have left matter more than broad similarity to earlier purchases; for tool hooks, usefulness depends on a secure mounting surface."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my workshop interests but missed the difference between useful project complements, supplies I may already have and specialized parts I do not currently need."
}"}
